<p><a href="https://jasonturner.arizona.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jason Turner</a>, currently professor of philosophy at the <a href="https://philosophy.arizona.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Arizona</a>, will be moving to the <a href="https://philosophy.nd.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Notre Dame</a>. <span id="more-57119"></span></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-57120 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/turner-jason-photo.png" alt="" width="470" height="440" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/turner-jason-photo.png 760w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/turner-jason-photo-300x281.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/turner-jason-photo-400x375.png 400w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 470px) 100vw, 470px" /></p>
<p>Professor Turner works in metaphysics, philosophy of action, and philosophy of logic. He is the author of <a href="https://academic.oup.com/book/25934" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>The Facts in Logical Space</em></a> and many other writings, which you can learn about <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/jason-turner" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
<p>He takes up his new position as professor of philosophy at the University of Notre Dame in the fall.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/04/13/turner-from-arizona-to-notre-dame/">Turner from Arizona to Notre Dame</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>